---
import InternalLayout from '../../layouts/InternalLayout.astro';
---
<InternalLayout title="Analytics">
  <div class="an-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Website</p>
      <h1>Analytics</h1>
      <p class="lede">Where visitors come from, what they read, and which of them ask for an estimate.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="an-hero-actions"><button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-refresh>Refresh</button></div>
  </div>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-pipe-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Your business</p><h2 id="an-pipe-h">Requests to revenue</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-pipe-window>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note">Counted from your own quotes, jobs and payments. These totals count every quote, including ones not linked to a website request, so each stage is its own count for the period, not the same customers followed through. The table below follows only linked quotes.</p>
    <div class="an-stats an-stats-5">
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Estimate requests</span><strong data-pipe="leads">—</strong><small>from the website form</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Quotes written</span><strong data-pipe="quotes">—</strong><small data-pipe="quotedValue">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Quotes signed</span><strong data-pipe="signed">—</strong><small data-pipe="signedValue">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Jobs</span><strong data-pipe="jobs">—</strong><small><span data-pipe="completed">—</span> completed</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Collected</span><strong data-pipe="collected">—</strong><small data-pipe="collectedNote">on jobs from this period</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="an-grid">
      <article class="an-panel an-wide"><h3>From request to paid job</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="pipeFunnel"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Rates</h3><div data-list="pipeRates"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Needs attention</h3><div data-list="pipeAttention"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Which sources bring paying work</h3>
        <p class="an-note" data-source-coverage>—</p>
        <div class="an-chart" data-chart="sourceSigned"></div>
        <div class="an-table-wrap">
          <table class="an-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Requests</th><th scope="col">Quotes</th><th scope="col">Signed</th><th scope="col">Signed $</th><th scope="col">Collected</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-source-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-leads-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Estimate requests</p><h2 id="an-leads-h">Where leads came from</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-leads-total>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note">Counted from the requests in your own database (first visit source), so it works without any analytics account.</p>
    <div class="an-grid">
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Source</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="leadSources"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>First page visited</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="leadLanding"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide"><h3>Requests per week</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="leadWeekly"></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-permit-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Public records</p><h2 id="an-permit-h">Permit leads</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-permit-window>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note">Building permits from Clark County and the City of Vancouver, joined to county parcel records and state contractor licenses. This is research, not customers: nothing here is a lead or a quote until you act on it. Contractor matches are by exact name, so check one before you call. Same-size window replacements usually need no permit, so these lists miss most simple replacement jobs.</p>
    <p class="an-callout" data-permit-message hidden></p>
    <div class="an-stats" data-permit-stats hidden>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>New-home permits</span><strong data-permit="newHomes">—</strong><small data-permit="newHomesNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Builders</span><strong data-permit="builders">—</strong><small data-permit="buildersNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Remodel and addition permits</span><strong data-permit="remodels">—</strong><small data-permit="remodelsNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Homes built 2011–2016</span><strong data-permit="young">—</strong><small>among those remodel permits</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="an-grid" data-permit-grid hidden>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>New-home permits per month</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitMonthly"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Biggest builders by permits</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitBuilders"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Builders and lot owners</h3>
        <p class="an-note">The lot owner is usually the builder or its project company; the permit applicant is often a permit service or engineer. "30 days" and "90 days" count permits issued in that time.</p>
        <div class="an-table-wrap">
          <table class="an-table an-table-wide">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Builder</th><th scope="col">Permits</th><th scope="col">30 days</th><th scope="col">90 days</th><th scope="col">Subdivisions</th><th scope="col">State license</th><th scope="col">Phone</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-builder-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Remodel permits: what fits</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitSignals"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Remodel permits: decade the home was built</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitDecades"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Remodel and addition list</h3>
        <p class="an-note">Owner names and mailing addresses come from the county assessor. Use them for mail, not unsolicited calls or texts: Washington restricts those. Best fit first; "fit" counts how many of five signals apply (single-family, owner applied, addition, permit in last 90 days, sold in last 2 years).</p>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-homeowners-load>Show the list</button>
        <div class="an-table-wrap" data-homeowners-wrap hidden>
          <table class="an-table an-table-wide">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Permit</th><th scope="col">Work</th><th scope="col">Built</th><th scope="col">Owner</th><th scope="col">Owner mail</th><th scope="col">Sold</th><th scope="col">Fit</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-homeowner-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-site-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Google Analytics</p><h2 id="an-site-h">Site traffic</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-ga4-state>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-callout" data-ga4-message hidden></p>
    <div class="an-stats" data-ga4-stats hidden>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Visitors</span><strong data-stat="users28">—</strong><small><span data-stat="users7">—</span> in last 7 days</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Sessions</span><strong data-stat="sessions28">—</strong><small><span data-stat="sessions7">—</span> in last 7 days</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Page views</span><strong data-stat="pageViews28">—</strong><small><span data-stat="pageViews7">—</span> in last 7 days</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Estimate requests</span><strong data-stat="leadEvents28">—</strong><small><span data-stat="leadEvents7">—</span> in last 7 days</small></article>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note" data-ga4-window hidden>Visitors, sessions and page views cover the last 28 days unless noted.</p>
    <div class="an-grid" data-ga4-lists hidden>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide"><h3>Sessions and visitors per day</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="ga4Daily"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Where sessions come from</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="channels"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Most viewed pages</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="topPages"></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-tools-h">
    <div class="an-head"><div><p class="kicker">Open in the source</p><h2 id="an-tools-h">Analytics tools</h2></div></div>
    <div class="an-links" data-links>
      <a class="an-link" data-link="ga4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Google Analytics</strong><span>Full reports</span></a>
      <a class="an-link" data-link="tagManager" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Google Tag Manager</strong><span>Tags and triggers (collects data, has no reports of its own)</span></a>
      <a class="an-link" data-link="searchConsole" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Search Console</strong><span>Search queries and indexing</span></a>
      <a class="an-link" data-link="ahrefsWebmasterTools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Ahrefs Webmaster Tools</strong><span>Backlinks and site health. The free plan has no API, so it opens in Ahrefs.</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="an-status" data-status role="status">Loading analytics…</p>
</InternalLayout>
<script>
  import { barChart, columnChart, donutChart, funnelChart, lineChart } from '../../lib/charts';

  type Row = { label: string; value: number };
  type Ga4 = {
    status: 'ok' | 'unconfigured' | 'unavailable';
    last7?: Record<string, number>;
    last28?: Record<string, number>;
    topPages?: Row[];
    channels?: Row[];
    daily?: { date: string; sessions: number; users: number }[];
  };
  type Leads = {
    status: 'ok' | 'unavailable';
    days?: number;
    total?: number;
    sources?: Row[];
    landingPages?: Row[];
    weekly?: { weekOf: string; value: number }[];
  };
  type Pipeline = {
    status: 'ok' | 'unavailable';
    days?: number;
    staleDraftDays?: number;
    leads?: number | null;
    quotes?: { created: number; quotedCents: number; signed: number; signedCents: number; staleDrafts: number; staleDraftCents: number; medianDaysToSign: number | null } | null;
    jobs?: { created: number; completed: number; collectedCents: number | null; otherWork?: { created: number; collectedCents: number | null } } | null;
    awaitingJob?: number | null;
    bySource?: {
      linkedQuotes: number;
      unlinkedQuotes: number;
      sources: { label: string; leads: number; quotes: number; signed: number; signedCents: number; collectedCents: number | null }[];
    } | null;
    rates?: { quotesPerLead: number | null; signedPerQuote: number | null };
  };
  type PermitBuilder = {
    name: string; applicants: string[]; permits: number; lots: number; subdivisions: string[]; jurisdictions: string[];
    lastIssued: string; issued30d: number; issued90d: number;
    license: { match: string; business: string; number: string; phone: string; address: string; principal: string; status: string; expires: string } | null;
  };
  type PermitSummary = {
    status: 'ok' | 'empty' | 'unavailable';
    meta?: Record<string, string>;
    homeowners?: { total: number; signals: { key: string; label: string; value: number }[]; decades: Row[]; absentee: number; built2011to2016: number };
    newHomes?: { permits: number; entities: number; repeatEntities: number; licenseMatched: number; byMonth: Row[] };
    builders?: PermitBuilder[];
  };
  type HomeownerLead = {
    id: string; permitDate: string; status: string; workType: string; address: string; yearBuilt: number | null; sqft: number | null;
    owner: string; ownerMailing: string; absentee: boolean; ownerApplied: boolean; lastSaleDate: string; lastSaleCents: number | null; signals: string[]; score: number;
  };
  type Payload = { ga4: Ga4; leads: Leads; pipeline?: Pipeline; links: Record<string, string> };

  const nf = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
  const money = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD', maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
  const dollars = (cents: number | null | undefined) => (typeof cents === 'number' ? money.format(cents / 100) : '—');
  const count = (value: number | null | undefined) => (typeof value === 'number' ? nf.format(value) : '—');
  const $ = (selector: string) => document.querySelector(selector);

  /**
   * Charts are drawn at the width their box actually has, so text stays readable
   * on a phone, and redrawn when that width changes. Each chart registers a
   * builder here; `paint()` runs them all.
   */
  type ChartJob = { build: (width: number) => string; empty: string };
  const jobs = new Map<string, ChartJob>();
  const widths = new Map<string, number>();

  // SVG from our own builders is parsed and imported as nodes; nothing is assigned as HTML.
  function mountSvg(host: HTMLElement, markup: string): boolean {
    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(markup, 'image/svg+xml');
    const root = doc.documentElement;
    if (!root || root.nodeName !== 'svg' || doc.querySelector('parsererror')) return false;
    host.replaceChildren(document.importNode(root, true));
    return true;
  }

  function paintOne(name: string, job: ChartJob) {
    const host = $(`[data-chart="${name}"]`);
    if (!(host instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    const width = Math.floor(host.clientWidth || host.parentElement?.clientWidth || 320);
    widths.set(name, width);
    const markup = job.build(width);
    if (markup && mountSvg(host, markup)) return;
    const p = document.createElement('p');
    p.className = 'an-empty';
    p.textContent = job.empty;
    host.replaceChildren(p);
  }

  function setChart(name: string, job: ChartJob) {
    jobs.set(name, job);
    paintOne(name, job);
  }

  function clearChart(name: string, message: string) {
    setChart(name, { build: () => '', empty: message });
  }

  let repaintQueued = false;
  function repaintOnResize() {
    if (repaintQueued) return;
    repaintQueued = true;
    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      repaintQueued = false;
      for (const [name, job] of jobs) {
        const host = $(`[data-chart="${name}"]`);
        if (host instanceof HTMLElement && Math.abs(host.clientWidth - (widths.get(name) ?? 0)) > 8) paintOne(name, job);
      }
    });
  }
  window.addEventListener('resize', repaintOnResize, { passive: true });

  function setText(selector: string, text: string) {
    const el = $(selector);
    if (el instanceof HTMLElement) el.textContent = text;
  }

  function show(selector: string, visible: boolean) {
    const el = $(selector);
    if (el instanceof HTMLElement) el.hidden = !visible;
  }

  function renderGa4(ga4: Ga4) {
    show('[data-ga4-stats]', false);
    show('[data-ga4-lists]', false);
    show('[data-ga4-window]', false);
    if (ga4.status === 'ok' && ga4.last7 && ga4.last28) {
      setText('[data-ga4-state]', 'Connected');
      show('[data-ga4-message]', false);
      show('[data-ga4-stats]', true);
      show('[data-ga4-lists]', true);
      show('[data-ga4-window]', true);
      for (const key of ['users', 'sessions', 'pageViews', 'leadEvents']) {
        setText(`[data-stat="${key}28"]`, nf.format(ga4.last28[key] ?? 0));
        setText(`[data-stat="${key}7"]`, nf.format(ga4.last7[key] ?? 0));
      }
      const daily = ga4.daily ?? [];
      const shortDay = (iso: string) => new Date(`${iso}T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' });
      setChart('ga4Daily', {
        build: (width) =>
          lineChart(
            [
              { name: 'Sessions', values: daily.map((d) => d.sessions) },
              { name: 'Visitors', values: daily.map((d) => d.users) },
            ],
            daily.map((d) => shortDay(d.date)),
            { width, title: 'Sessions and visitors per day, last 28 days' },
          ),
        empty: 'No daily traffic recorded yet.',
      });
      setChart('channels', {
        build: (width) => donutChart(ga4.channels, { width, title: 'Sessions by channel, last 28 days', centerLabel: 'sessions' }),
        empty: 'No sessions recorded yet.',
      });
      setChart('topPages', {
        build: (width) => barChart(ga4.topPages, { width, title: 'Most viewed pages, last 28 days' }),
        empty: 'No page views recorded yet.',
      });
      return;
    }
    show('[data-ga4-message]', true);
    if (ga4.status === 'unconfigured') {
      setText('[data-ga4-state]', 'Not connected');
      setText('[data-ga4-message]', 'Google Analytics is not connected to this page yet. See the Analytics setup section in internal/README.md.');
    } else {
      setText('[data-ga4-state]', 'Unavailable');
      setText('[data-ga4-message]', 'Google Analytics did not respond. Try Refresh in a minute; the lead numbers above are unaffected.');
    }
  }

  function renderTextList(name: string, lines: [string, string][]) {
    const host = $(`[data-list="${name}"]`);
    if (!(host instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    host.replaceChildren();
    for (const [labelText, valueText] of lines) {
      const item = document.createElement('div');
      item.className = 'an-row';
      const label = document.createElement('span');
      label.className = 'an-row-label';
      label.textContent = labelText;
      const value = document.createElement('strong');
      value.textContent = valueText;
      item.append(label, value);
      host.append(item);
    }
  }

  function renderPipeline(pipe: Pipeline | undefined) {
    if (!pipe || pipe.status !== 'ok') {
      setText('[data-pipe-window]', 'Unavailable');
      // Never leave numbers from an earlier load on screen after a failed refresh.
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-pipe]').forEach((el) => {
        if (el instanceof HTMLElement) el.textContent = '—';
      });
      renderTextList('pipeRates', [['Business data could not be loaded.', '']]);
      renderTextList('pipeAttention', []);
      clearChart('pipeFunnel', 'Business data could not be loaded.');
      return;
    }
    const q = pipe.quotes;
    const j = pipe.jobs;
    const pct = (value: number | null | undefined) => (typeof value === 'number' ? `${value}%` : '—');
    setText('[data-pipe-window]', `Last ${pipe.days ?? 90} days`);
    setText('[data-pipe="leads"]', count(pipe.leads));
    setText('[data-pipe="quotes"]', count(q?.created));
    setText('[data-pipe="quotedValue"]', q ? `${dollars(q.quotedCents)} quoted` : '—');
    setText('[data-pipe="signed"]', count(q?.signed));
    setText('[data-pipe="signedValue"]', q ? `${dollars(q.signedCents)} signed` : '—');
    setText('[data-pipe="jobs"]', count(j?.created));
    setText('[data-pipe="completed"]', count(j?.completed));
    setText('[data-pipe="collected"]', dollars(j?.collectedCents));
    const other = j?.otherWork;
    setText('[data-pipe="collectedNote"]', other && other.created > 0 ? `on jobs from this period, incl. ${other.created} non-window job${other.created === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : 'on jobs from this period');
    const stages = [
      { label: 'Requests', value: pipe.leads },
      { label: 'Quotes written', value: q?.created },
      { label: 'Quotes signed', value: q?.signed },
      { label: 'Jobs', value: j?.created },
    ].filter((stage): stage is { label: string; value: number } => typeof stage.value === 'number');
    setChart('pipeFunnel', {
      build: (width) => (stages.some((stage) => stage.value > 0) ? funnelChart(stages, { width, title: `Requests to jobs, last ${pipe.days ?? 90} days` }) : ''),
      empty: 'Nothing to chart yet in this period.',
    });
    const avgSigned = q && q.signed > 0 ? dollars(Math.round(q.signedCents / q.signed)) : '—';
    renderTextList('pipeRates', [
      ['Quotes written per estimate request', pct(pipe.rates?.quotesPerLead)],
      ['Quotes signed per quote written', pct(pipe.rates?.signedPerQuote)],
      ['Typical days from quote to signature', typeof q?.medianDaysToSign === 'number' ? `${q.medianDaysToSign} days` : '—'],
      ['Average signed quote', avgSigned],
    ]);
    const stale = q?.staleDrafts ?? 0;
    renderTextList('pipeAttention', [
      [`Draft quotes older than ${pipe.staleDraftDays ?? 14} days`, q ? `${nf.format(stale)}${stale ? ` · ${dollars(q.staleDraftCents)}` : ''}` : '—'],
      ['Finalized quotes not yet a job', count(pipe.awaitingJob)],
    ]);
  }

  function renderSources(pipe: Pipeline | undefined) {
    const body = $('[data-source-rows]');
    if (!(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    body.replaceChildren();
    const data = pipe?.status === 'ok' ? pipe.bySource : null;
    if (!data) {
      setText('[data-source-coverage]', 'Source data could not be loaded.');
      clearChart('sourceSigned', 'Source data could not be loaded.');
      return;
    }
    const signedRows = data.sources.filter((row) => row.signedCents > 0).map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row.signedCents }));
    setChart('sourceSigned', {
      build: (width) => barChart(signedRows, { width, title: 'Signed quote value by source', format: dollars }),
      empty: 'No signed quotes are linked to a source yet.',
    });
    const total = data.linkedQuotes + data.unlinkedQuotes;
    setText(
      '[data-source-coverage]',
      total
        ? `${nf.format(data.linkedQuotes)} of ${nf.format(total)} quotes from this period are linked to a website request. Link the others from each quote's page to credit their source.`
        : 'No quotes in this period yet.',
    );
    if (!data.sources.length) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const td = document.createElement('td');
      td.colSpan = 6;
      td.className = 'an-empty';
      td.textContent = 'No website requests or linked quotes yet.';
      tr.append(td);
      body.append(tr);
      return;
    }
    for (const row of data.sources) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const cells = [row.label, nf.format(row.leads), nf.format(row.quotes), nf.format(row.signed), dollars(row.signedCents), dollars(row.collectedCents)];
      cells.forEach((text, i) => {
        const cell = document.createElement(i === 0 ? 'th' : 'td');
        if (i === 0) cell.setAttribute('scope', 'row');
        cell.textContent = text;
        tr.append(cell);
      });
      body.append(tr);
    }
  }

  function renderLeads(leads: Leads) {
    if (leads.status !== 'ok') {
      setText('[data-leads-total]', 'Unavailable');
      for (const name of ['leadSources', 'leadLanding', 'leadWeekly']) clearChart(name, 'Lead data could not be loaded.');
      return;
    }
    const total = leads.total ?? 0;
    setText('[data-leads-total]', `${nf.format(total)} in the last ${leads.days ?? 90} days`);
    const weekLabel = (iso: string) => new Date(`${iso}T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' });
    const weekly = (leads.weekly ?? []).map((week) => ({ label: weekLabel(week.weekOf), value: week.value }));
    setChart('leadSources', {
      build: (width) => donutChart(leads.sources, { width, title: 'Estimate requests by source', centerLabel: 'requests' }),
      empty: 'No estimate requests yet.',
    });
    setChart('leadLanding', {
      build: (width) => barChart(leads.landingPages, { width, title: 'Estimate requests by first page visited' }),
      empty: 'No estimate requests yet.',
    });
    setChart('leadWeekly', {
      build: (width) => (weekly.some((week) => week.value > 0) ? columnChart(weekly, { width, title: 'Estimate requests per week (week starting)' }) : ''),
      empty: 'No estimate requests yet.',
    });
  }

  const shortDate = (iso: string) => (/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(iso) ? new Date(`${iso}T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: '2-digit' }) : '—');
  const monthLabel = (ym: string) => (/^\d{4}-\d{2}$/.test(ym) ? new Date(`${ym}-01T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short' }) : ym);

  function appendRow(body: HTMLElement, cells: (string | HTMLElement)[]) {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    cells.forEach((value, i) => {
      const cell = document.createElement(i === 0 ? 'th' : 'td');
      if (i === 0) cell.setAttribute('scope', 'row');
      if (typeof value === 'string') cell.textContent = value;
      else cell.append(value);
      tr.append(cell);
    });
    body.append(tr);
  }

  // Phone numbers come from a public license record as 10 digits; anything else is shown as plain text, never linked.
  function phoneCell(raw: string): string | HTMLElement {
    const digits = raw.replace(/\D/g, '');
    if (digits.length !== 10) return raw || '—';
    const link = document.createElement('a');
    link.href = `tel:+1${digits}`;
    link.textContent = `(${digits.slice(0, 3)}) ${digits.slice(3, 6)}-${digits.slice(6)}`;
    return link;
  }

  function renderPermits(permit: PermitSummary | undefined) {
    const message = $('[data-permit-message]');
    const hide = () => { show('[data-permit-stats]', false); show('[data-permit-grid]', false); };
    if (!permit || permit.status !== 'ok' || !permit.homeowners || !permit.newHomes) {
      hide();
      show('[data-permit-message]', true);
      setText('[data-permit-window]', permit?.status === 'empty' ? 'Not loaded' : 'Unavailable');
      if (message instanceof HTMLElement) {
        message.textContent = permit?.status === 'empty'
          ? 'No permit data has been loaded yet. Build it with npm run build:permit-leads, then load the SQL file into the database. See the Permit leads section of internal/README.md.'
          : 'Permit data could not be loaded. Try Refresh; the rest of this page is unaffected.';
      }
      return;
    }
    const h = permit.homeowners;
    const n = permit.newHomes;
    show('[data-permit-message]', false);
    show('[data-permit-stats]', true);
    show('[data-permit-grid]', true);
    const meta = permit.meta ?? {};
    setText('[data-permit-window]', `${shortDate(meta.window_start ?? '')} to ${shortDate(meta.window_end ?? '')} · loaded ${shortDate((meta.imported_at ?? '').slice(0, 10))}`);
    setText('[data-permit="newHomes"]', count(n.permits));
    setText('[data-permit="newHomesNote"]', `across ${nf.format(n.entities)} lot owners`);
    setText('[data-permit="builders"]', count(n.repeatEntities));
    setText('[data-permit="buildersNote"]', `with 2+ permits · ${nf.format(n.licenseMatched)} matched to a state license`);
    setText('[data-permit="remodels"]', count(h.total));
    setText('[data-permit="remodelsNote"]', `${nf.format(h.absentee)} where the owner lives elsewhere`);
    setText('[data-permit="young"]', count(h.built2011to2016));
    const builders = permit.builders ?? [];
    setChart('permitMonthly', {
      build: (width) => (n.byMonth.length ? columnChart(n.byMonth.map((r) => ({ label: monthLabel(r.label), value: r.value })), { width, title: 'New-home permits issued per month' }) : ''),
      empty: 'No new-home permits in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitBuilders', {
      build: (width) => barChart(builders.slice(0, 8).map((b) => ({ label: b.name, value: b.permits })), { width, title: 'Builders by new-home permits' }),
      empty: 'No builders in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitSignals', {
      build: (width) => barChart(h.signals.map((s) => ({ label: s.label, value: s.value })), { width, title: 'Remodel permits by fit signal' }),
      empty: 'No remodel permits in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitDecades', {
      build: (width) => (h.decades.length ? columnChart(h.decades, { width, title: 'Remodel permits by decade the home was built' }) : ''),
      empty: 'No year-built data.',
    });
    const body = $('[data-builder-rows]');
    if (!(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    body.replaceChildren();
    if (!builders.length) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const td = document.createElement('td');
      td.colSpan = 7;
      td.className = 'an-empty';
      td.textContent = 'No builders in this window.';
      tr.append(td);
      body.append(tr);
      return;
    }
    for (const b of builders) {
      const license = b.license;
      const licenseText = license
        ? `${license.business} · ${license.number}${license.status && license.status !== 'ACTIVE' ? ` · ${license.status}` : ''}${/verify/.test(license.match) ? ' · name match, verify' : ''}`
        : 'None found by exact name';
      appendRow(body, [b.name, nf.format(b.permits), nf.format(b.issued30d), nf.format(b.issued90d), b.subdivisions.join(', ') || '—', licenseText, license ? phoneCell(license.phone) : '—']);
    }
  }

  async function loadPermits() {
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/internal/api/permit-leads', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('bad status');
      renderPermits((await response.json()) as PermitSummary);
    } catch {
      renderPermits(undefined);
    }
  }

  let homeownersShown = false;
  async function loadHomeowners() {
    const button = $('[data-homeowners-load]');
    const body = $('[data-homeowner-rows]');
    if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement) || !(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    if (homeownersShown) {
      homeownersShown = false;
      show('[data-homeowners-wrap]', false);
      button.textContent = 'Show the list';
      return;
    }
    button.disabled = true;
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/internal/api/permit-leads?view=homeowners&limit=150', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('bad status');
      const rows = ((await response.json()) as { rows?: HomeownerLead[] }).rows ?? [];
      body.replaceChildren();
      for (const r of rows) {
        const mail = r.ownerMailing ? (r.absentee ? `Elsewhere: ${r.ownerMailing}` : 'At the property') : '—';
        const sold = r.lastSaleDate ? `${shortDate(r.lastSaleDate)}${typeof r.lastSaleCents === 'number' ? ` · ${dollars(r.lastSaleCents)}` : ''}` : '—';
        appendRow(body, [r.address || '(no address)', shortDate(r.permitDate), r.workType || '—', r.yearBuilt ? String(r.yearBuilt) : '—', `${r.owner || '—'}${r.ownerApplied ? ' (applied)' : ''}`, mail, sold, `${r.score} of 5`]);
      }
      if (!rows.length) {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        const td = document.createElement('td');
        td.colSpan = 8;
        td.className = 'an-empty';
        td.textContent = 'No remodel permits loaded.';
        tr.append(td);
        body.append(tr);
      }
      homeownersShown = true;
      show('[data-homeowners-wrap]', true);
      button.textContent = 'Hide the list';
    } catch {
      setText('[data-status]', 'Could not load the permit list. Try again.');
    } finally {
      button.disabled = false;
    }
  }

  async function load() {
    setText('[data-status]', 'Loading analytics…');
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/internal/api/analytics', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      if (response.status === 401 || response.redirected) {
        location.href = '/internal/login?next=/internal/analytics';
        return;
      }
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('bad status');
      const data = (await response.json()) as Payload;
      renderPipeline(data.pipeline);
      renderSources(data.pipeline);
      renderLeads(data.leads);
      renderGa4(data.ga4);
      void loadPermits();
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-link]').forEach((el) => {
        const href = data.links?.[(el as HTMLElement).dataset.link || ''];
        if (el instanceof HTMLAnchorElement && typeof href === 'string' && /^https:\/\//.test(href)) el.href = href;
      });
      setText('[data-status]', `Updated ${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()}`);
    } catch {
      setText('[data-status]', 'Could not load analytics. Try Refresh.');
    }
  }

  document.querySelector('[data-homeowners-load]')?.addEventListener('click', loadHomeowners);
  document.querySelector('[data-refresh]')?.addEventListener('click', load);
  load();
</script>
<style>
  .an-hero{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:var(--space-m);margin-bottom:var(--space-m)}
  .an-hero h1{margin:.08rem 0 .35rem}
  .an-section{margin-bottom:var(--space-l)}
  .an-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:var(--space-s);margin-bottom:.4rem}
  .an-head h2{margin:.1rem 0 0}
  .an-meta{font-size:var(--step--2);font-weight:750;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .an-note{margin:0 0 var(--space-s);color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-callout{margin:0 0 var(--space-s);padding:.85rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--paper-sunk);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:var(--space-s)}
  .an-wide{grid-column:1/-1}
  .an-panel{min-width:0;padding:1rem 1.05rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised);box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)}
  .an-panel h3{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:var(--step-0)}
  /* Rows are built by script after load, so Astro's scoped-style attribute is absent; these must be global. */
  :global(.an-row){position:relative;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.75rem;padding:.55rem 0 .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  :global(.an-row:last-child){border-bottom:0}
  :global(.an-row-label){min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:var(--step--1)}
  :global(.an-row strong){font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.an-row i){position:absolute;left:0;bottom:.3rem;height:3px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--accent);opacity:.55}
  :global(.an-empty){margin:0;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  /* Charts are built by script (see src/lib/charts.ts), so these must be global. */
  :global(.an-chart){min-width:0}
  :global(svg.ch){--ch-1:var(--accent);--ch-2:#3a3d42;--ch-3:#b7791f;--ch-4:#2b6cb0;--ch-5:#b83280;--ch-6:#8a8d93;display:block;width:100%;height:auto;overflow:visible;font-family:inherit}
  :global(.ch-label){font-size:12px;fill:var(--ink)}
  :global(.ch-axis){font-size:11px;fill:var(--ink-soft)}
  :global(.ch-value){font-size:12px;font-weight:650;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.ch-center){font-size:20px;font-weight:700;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.ch-barvalue){font-size:12px;font-weight:700;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;paint-order:stroke;stroke:var(--paper-raised);stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round}
  :global(.ch-grid){stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1}
  :global(.ch-track){fill:var(--paper-sunk)}
  :global(.ch-zero){fill:var(--line-strong)}
  :global(.ch-bar){fill:var(--c,var(--ch-1))}
  :global(.ch-f0){opacity:.55}:global(.ch-f1){opacity:.7}:global(.ch-f2){opacity:.85}:global(.ch-f3){opacity:1}
  :global(.ch-s0){--c:var(--ch-1)}:global(.ch-s1){--c:var(--ch-2)}:global(.ch-s2){--c:var(--ch-3)}:global(.ch-s3){--c:var(--ch-4)}:global(.ch-s4){--c:var(--ch-5)}:global(.ch-s5){--c:var(--ch-6)}
  :global(.ch-line){stroke:var(--c);stroke-width:2;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-linecap:round}
  :global(.ch-area){fill:var(--c);opacity:.12}
  :global(.ch-arc){stroke:var(--c)}
  :global(.ch-swatch),:global(.ch-dot){fill:var(--c)}
  :global(.ch-hit){fill:transparent}
  :global(.ch-hit:hover){fill:rgb(0 0 0 / .05)}
  .an-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem;margin-bottom:var(--space-xs)}
  .an-stat{display:grid;gap:.25rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised)}
  .an-stat>span{font-size:var(--step--2);font-weight:750;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .an-stat strong{font-size:var(--step-3);line-height:1;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .an-stat small{color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .an-links{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem}
  .an-link{display:grid;gap:.2rem;padding:.95rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised);color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
  .an-link:hover,.an-link:focus-visible{border-color:var(--accent)}
  .an-link span{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-status{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}
  /* Keep the source column readable on a phone; the wrapper scrolls sideways instead of crushing it. */
  .an-table{min-width:32rem;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--step--1);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.an-table th),:global(.an-table td){padding:.5rem .4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}
  :global(.an-table th[scope="row"]),.an-table thead th:first-child{text-align:left;white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-width:7rem}
  .an-table-wide{min-width:54rem}
  .an-table-wide thead th:nth-child(5),.an-table-wide thead th:nth-child(6){text-align:left}
  :global(.an-table a){color:inherit;text-decoration:underline}
  :global(.an-table td:nth-child(5)),:global(.an-table td:nth-child(6)){text-align:left;white-space:normal;min-width:9rem}
  .an-stats-5{grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr))}
  @media(max-width:900px){.an-stats-5{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.an-stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
  @media(max-width:720px){.an-hero{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.an-grid,.an-links{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
  @media(max-width:420px){.an-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
